Apache-2.0. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.

data/base-7620-word.json.gz and data/invoice-7620.json are the unmodified
data/word.json.gz and data/invoice.json of research/p104-stationary-primal-dual
at SYLforge's #7620, vendored as data only; data/affected-pairs-7620.json is
the 837-pair affected census pinned in that package's runners/native.py,
copied as data. #7620 is SYLforge's composition of the 167-CLEAR stationary
primal/dual bypasses on #7616 (candidate work with Claude Opus 5.5 and
Antigravity, validation with OpenAI assistance) and builds on #7616, Ali
Romman's #7605 (with OpenAI Codex), our #7611 stay drops (DreamingOfClouds with
Claude), Clear1nsight's #7612 contact rechart, Hao Yan/FanPUYen's #7604,
SYLforge's #7603, ToikY's #7546/#7544, Rohan Arun's signed #7113 caller and all
contributors named in those packages. Our #7615 and #7617 supply the courier
lineage on earlier bases.

The courier (funded-return) move pattern is the crowd's: Clear1nsight's
#7244/#7274/#7314/#7334/#7481 funded-return chain and determinant-one
co-encoding, rohanarun's #7480 bypass and #7277, CubeJerry's #7577 ceiling
analysis, and petalas's #7326. This package applies that pattern to one
(transit, courier) pair on #7620 and re-stops one helper.

check.py adapts the replay checks of our #7617 package. Its column-test section
is written from the description of the affected-pair tests in #7620's README and
native runner (512 forward and 512 adjoint Gaussian columns, signed Pauli action,
absolute phase, wrong-phase rejection); the Gaussian-dyadic Clifford conventions
(gate set P/D/C/X/phase, canonical frame circuit, child recipe) follow the
repository's frozen interpreter and compiler documented in main. It imports no
other package and none of the other PRs' code was run.
